00:53:22.075 --> 00:53:30.955
workflow? Yeah, so it's going to be a daunting thing if you already have a big complex shiny

00:53:30.955 --> 00:53:39.754
application to undertake the project as though you want to export all the code in the shiny app,

00:53:39.754 --> 00:53:47.034
that's going to be a difficult undertaking if you kind of approach it that way. But if you break it

00:53:47.034 --> 00:53:52.715
down into smaller pieces and just say this is an important output that I want to provide

00:53:52.715 --> 00:53:59.514
reproducible code for, the way you could kind of approach it is, you know, maybe you identify this

00:53:59.514 --> 00:54:07.514
output summary as an important output and that's being created through this render print reactive

00:54:07.514 --> 00:54:14.794
context. The first thing to do would be to change this render print into a meta render which allows

00:54:14.794 --> 00:54:19.914
this render context to then have this ability to sort of spit out code at the end.

00:54:22.555 --> 00:54:28.955
And then identify any reactive reads in that reactive expression. So the read of this bare

00:54:28.955 --> 00:54:34.874
reactive expression should then get the dot dot operator and then you just add that to all the

00:54:34.874 --> 00:54:41.675
reactive reads in this expression. And then you'll want to go back to all these reactive reads that

00:54:41.675 --> 00:54:48.634
you've marked with the dot dot operator and follow them back to the original creation.

00:54:49.595 --> 00:54:57.114
And in the case of reactive, we have a meta reactive variant which works just like reactive

00:54:57.114 --> 00:55:05.994
in the normal execution context but also gives it the ability to generate code when you call it

00:55:05.994 --> 00:55:12.235
inside of this expand chain context. Interesting. So it's kind of like working

00:55:12.874 --> 00:55:19.034
backwards in the sense of like identifying an output and then identifying all the dependencies

00:55:19.034 --> 00:55:25.435
